  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liquid Gold: Demonstrating Dry Sanitation and Liquid waste Seperation Solutions in South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dutch- South African company LiquidGold (LG) has developed a technology to &#x2018;harvest&#x2019; human waste (urine and faeces) and convert these into a market-ready and highly valuable fertilizer (Pure Gold). It uses a dry sanitation, 100% waterless, urinate only gender-neutral toilet fitted in an E-Container with a bio-reactor technology to enable a valuable self-sustaining system. The technology prevents waste from ending up in wastewater treatment plants, reduces water consumption, costs and emissions, saves energy, improves hygiene and promotes environmental awareness. Furthermore, it allows for new income streams and provides sanitation in areas where proper sanitation currently is limited. To prepare for future investments in a local production facility and to demonstrate the functionality of its waterless toilets in South Africa, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provided support. The project included the installation of two E-Containers at two public schools, the testing of 1,000 litres of processed waste and treated water with the mobile reactor, reporting on test results (water, sewage and carbon savings), training of local facility managers and the development of a bankable business plan. The project supported 5 direct jobs, 4 indirect jobs and provided sustainable knowledge transfer by training 8 people. The project was successful and further investments are currently being prepared.</narrative>
  </description>
